  "calculations": {
    "rebasing": "To rebase any index series at year b: X_t/X_b*100. For percent cumulative change subtract 100.",
    "gdp_real_percap_index2020": "100 * GDP_real_percap_eur2020_t / GDP_real_percap_eur2020_2020",
    "implied_population_index2020": "100 * GDP_volume_index2020_t / GDP_real_percap_index2020_t",
    "household_consumption_real_percap_index2020_approx": "100 * Household_consumption_volume_index2020_t / Implied_population_index2020_t",
    "equivalent_formula": "Household_consumption_volume_index2020_t / GDP_volume_index2020_t * GDP_real_percap_index2020_t",
    "limitation": "Derived consumption per capita is an APPROXIMATE own calculation, not an Idescat published series. It uses the population implicit in the published real-GDP-per-capita series and the same annual accounts revision. Source indices rounded to 0.1 imply small rounding errors. Preserve full precision for calculations; display 1 decimal.",
    "concepts": "GDP, income, consumption are FLOWS, not wealth (assets minus liabilities). GDP/capita and consumption/capita are means, not distributions/medians. Household consumption is private households only; NPISH consumption included with general government in this Idescat demand classification. Do not label it total individual actual consumption including public health/education."
